-- title:
--   Tate's trace estimate in the p-cyclotomic tower
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $m$ be a natural number. Write $\mathrm{cyclotomicTower}\,p\,n$ for the intermediate field of the fixed algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl p` of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}_p$ the set of all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{p^n}=1$, i.e. the subfield generated by the $p^n$-th roots of unity. Let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of `PadicAlgCl p` as a $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra which lies in the fixing subgroup of $\mathrm{cyclotomicTower}\,p\,(m+2)$, that is, $\sigma$ fixes every element of $\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^{m+2}})$, but does not lie in the fixing subgroup of $\mathrm{cyclotomicTower}\,p\,(m+3)$, so $\sigma$ moves some element of $\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^{m+3}})$. Then for every $y$ belonging to $\mathrm{cyclotomicTower}\,p\,(m+3)$ one has the estimate
--   $$\Big\| \sum_{i=0}^{p-1} \sigma^i(y) \Big\| \le \|(p:\mathbb{Q}_p)\| \cdot p^{1/((p-1)p^{m+1})} \cdot \|y\|,$$
--   the norms being the $p$-adic absolute values on `PadicAlgCl p` and on $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (so $\|(p:\mathbb{Q}_p)\| = p^{-1}$), the sum being indexed by `Finset.range p`, and the middle factor being the real power of $p$ with exponent $1/((p-1)p^{m+1}) = 1/\varphi(p^{m+2})$.
--
--   Since the restriction of $\sigma$ generates the cyclic group of order $p$ that is $\mathrm{Gal}(\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^{m+3}})/\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^{m+2}}))$, the displayed sum is the relative trace of $y$, and the inequality is Tate's bound showing that the normalised traces up the $p$-cyclotomic tower are uniformly contracting. It is used in the construction of the Tate trace on the completion of the tower, in [`PadicComplex.exists_isTateTrace_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicComplex.exists_isTateTrace_cyclotomicTower), and its proof invokes [`PadicAlgCl.finrank_cyclotomicTower_and_pow_mem_fixingSubgroup`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.finrank_cyclotomicTower_and_pow_mem_fixingSubgroup) for the degrees of the cyclotomic layers and for the behaviour of $\sigma^p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PadicAlgCl_norm_sum_pow_apply_le_of_mem_cyclotomicTower.lean

